let __v_86 = Value::from("Load it so it can be tipped in one go, and put the awkward things on top: a car load usually drives straight in, but many sites ask for proof of address, and a van or a trailer is often booked. Paint, chemicals, gas bottles, batteries and anything with a screen go to a staffed container or to a steward rather than into a skip, so ask at the gate. Soil, rubble and plasterboard are usually limited to a few bags a visit. If you cannot drive it there, the council's bulky waste collection is the other route: usually charged, booked online or by phone, and they take it from the doorstep.");
